 "notes": "Boxes are the PDF widgets (3 pages). Widget names are misleading for the Yes/No pairs: on page 0 the widget named after the question ('Born US Citizen', 'Have you previously applied...', 'Do you have a valid (commercial) drivers license') is the YES box and 'Yes'/'Yes_2'/'Yes_3'/'Yes_4' is the NO box; on page 2 'Yes_7' is YES and 'toggle_6' is NO. YES boxes get bool_to_check, NO boxes equals. The two page-2 radio groups (group_1 = may we contact present employer, undefined_4 = temporary employment) each have one widget name for both kids, so one entry covers the Yes and the No kid; it has no transforms because the right op differs per kid. The two employer blocks on page 1 map to employment_history[] columns (one block per item). Pathless by design: 'Date of Employment' in each employer block (one blank fed by start and end date, which a single table column cannot express), the three certification bullets (list items), and the signature."
